  "result": "Excellent! All 215 tests pass (16 new credit note tests added). Here's what I implemented:\n\n**Updated src/errors.js** \u2014 Added CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error code.\n\n**Created src/credits.js** with `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` that:\n- Only works on issued invoices (status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid')\n- Returns NOT_ISSUED for draft invoices\n- Validates amount is a positive integer (returns AMOUNT_INVALID if not)\n- Validates amount doesn't exceed invoice total (returns CREDIT_TOO_HIGH if it does)\n- Returns `ok(creditNote)` with:\n  - `number`: generated with CN prefix (CN-YYYY-NNNN format)\n  - `invoiceNumber`: from the invoice\n  - `customerId`: from the invoice\n  - `amount`, `reason`, `date`: from input\n- Credit note numbers use separate counter from invoices\n- Handles mixed invoice/credit note numbers in existingNumbers\n\n**Created test/credits.test.js** with 16 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Basic credit note creation (issued invoices)\n- Status validation (draft rejected, issued/partially_paid/paid accepted)\n- Amount validation (non-integer, zero, negative rejected; equal to total accepted)\n- Credit limits (exceeding total rejected)\n- Numbering (separate from invoices, handles gaps, correct year)\n- Mixed number types\n- Multiple credit notes in same year\n- Different credit note year from invoice year\n- Data preservation\n- Invoices with discounts and VAT\n- Input immutability\n\nAll 215 tests pass successfully.",
